Build Specification — App 1: STAG Annotation Editor
Completeness status: COMPLETE. All sections delivered in one pass. No truncation. Formatted for copy-paste into another conversation window. No tables, no boxes.

What It Is
A desktop or web application where one annotator builds one STAG (Scale-Transition Annotation Graph) annotation record from start to finish. It walks the annotator through the specification's panels in order, enforces every schema rule, derives the display label and the anchoring status automatically, reports them together, and refuses to save a record that breaks a schema rule.

Core Requirements
Functional requirements:

Walk the annotator through panels in specification order (Artifact 1, Section 7; Artifact 2, Appendix B).

Enforce the node identity tuple rule: N = (S, M, G).

Enforce the M-equivalence witness requirement (Rule 24).

Enforce regime fallbacks (Rule 20).

Enforce the entailment basis decision tree (Artifact 1, Section 7.3).

Enforce the scale-separation record requirements (Artifact 1, Section 7.5).

Enforce the partition audit (Rules 7, 26; Artifact 1, Sections 5.8, 7.7, 7.8).

Derive the display label automatically (Artifact 1, Section 7.6).

Derive the evidential anchoring status automatically (Artifact 1, Section 1.2; Rule 29).

Report display label and anchoring status together in every rendering (Artifact 1, Section 7.10).

Refuse to save a record that breaks any of the 32 semantic rules (Artifact 2, Appendix B.2).

Non-functional requirements:

Single-annotator, single-record workflow.

Usable by domain scientists, ontology engineers, research groups.

Output compatible with JSON Schema and SHACL schema (Artifact 2).

Reproducible: same inputs produce same outputs.

Deterministic derivation: no randomness in label or anchoring computation.

Input Specification
Declared partition. Partition ID, version, domain entries, partition kind, admissibility status, justification. Required.

Declared granularity. The G component of the node tuple. Required.

Candidate descriptions. Each with S, M, G components. Required.

Matching rules. Pre-registered rules for S, M, G matching. Required.

M-equivalence rule version. Version of the exact-reparametrization rule. Required.

Model reference. The model or formalism. Required.

Theory version. Theory/model version under which annotation is produced. Required.

Annotator provenance. Annotator ID, date, affiliation. Required.

Existing annotation. For revision or supersession workflows. Optional.

Output Specification
Annotation record. JSON, conforming to JSON Schema (Artifact 2, Appendix B.1).

PROV-O serialization. Turtle or JSON-LD. Optional.

SHACL validation report. Text or JSON. Pass or violations with rule numbers.

Display label. Text. One of seven labels.

Evidential anchoring status. Text. One of six values.

Unclassified reason. Text. If label is STAG-Unclassified.

Flags. Booleans: not_determinable_flag, provisional_flag, threshold_sensitive_flag, regime_not_determinable, identity_partition_sensitive.

Audit log. Text or JSON. Rules checked, fields populated, flags attached.

Panel-by-Panel Specification
Panel 1: Setup and Pre-Registration
Fields: annotation_id; theory_version; annotator; annotation_date; partition_registry_id; partition_version; partition_kind; partition_admissibility_status; partition_preregistration_date; partition_justification; domain entries; granularity G; matching rules for S, M, G; m_equivalence_rule_version; model_reference.

Rules enforced: Rule 9 (declare matching rules, M-equivalence rule, granularity, partition justification before node identity finalized); Rule 11 (identify theory/model/version); Rule 6 (domain entries belong to partition); Artifact 1 Section 8.2 (admissibility criteria).

Validation: Partition must be admissible or flagged framework-level. If framework-level, warn that cross-domain counterfactual claims will be Untestable (Rule 4).

Panel 2: Candidate Descriptions and Node Identity
Fields: For each candidate: S, M, G; primary_observable; domains_spanned; validity_regime; solution_method_attribute; purpose_attribute; component-level match decisions; node_identity (merged, new_node, uncertain, not_determinable); m_equivalence_basis; m_equivalence_witness.

Rules enforced: Rule 8; Rule 16; Rule 14; Rule 24; Artifact 1 Section 5.3 (S/M/G matching rules; truncation rules; integrating out rules).

Validation: Merged decision with different Lagrangians and missing m_equivalence_basis or m_equivalence_witness is a validation error. If S, M, G all match, force merged. If any component does not match, offer new_node or uncertain.

Panel 3: Regime Attribute
Fields: regime_attribute.value; domain_specific_label; framework_value_mapping; order_parameter; control_parameter_point; phase_diagram_source; value_bands_if_crossover; regime_band_source; regime_band_analyst_chosen.

Rules enforced: Rule 15; Rule 20; Artifact 1 Section 5.2.

Validation: If symmetric, broken, or crossover-band, require order_parameter, control_parameter_point, phase_diagram_source. If phase_diagram_source unavailable, force not_determinable and attach flag. If regime_band_source = analyst_chosen, regime_band_analyst_chosen must be true.

Panel 4: Effective-Description Change
Fields: effective_description_change (Yes-strong, Yes-weak, No, Uncertain); effective_description_change_kind; evidence per criterion; external_justification for ΔAPP and ΔEFT; EXPERT expert records.

Rules enforced: Artifact 1 Section 4.1 (ΔDOF, ΔPC, ΔSYM, ΔAPP, ΔEFT, ΔCOL, ΔBIND, EXPERT definitions); Section 4.2 (Yes-strong, Yes-weak, No, Uncertain); Rule 5; Rule 23.

Validation: If ΔDOF fires alone, set Yes-weak. If ΔAPP or ΔEFT fires, require external_justification. If EXPERT fires, require at least three expert records.

Panel 5: Intervention Classification and Entailment Basis
Fields: intervention_classification; entailment_basis; cited_structural_result; cited_numerical_result; intervention_source_domains; intervention_target_domain; intervention_kind; defining_coupling_intervention; cross_domain_intervention_available; reason_if_not_performed.

Rules enforced: Artifact 1 Section 7.1 (E1 to E4 definitions and mapping); Section 7.3 (decision tree); Rule 18; Rule 31.

Validation: Decision tree implemented as wizard. If annotator cannot decide, log and require second rater. If cited_structural_result required but missing, refuse. If any applicability condition lacks witness, force E4.

Panel 6: Cross-Domain Counterfactual Dependence and Material-Change Test
Fields: cross_domain_counterfactual_dependence; model_reference; counterfactual_intervention; counterfactual_description; counterfactual_result; material_change_test; material_change_test_justification; material_change_result; quantities_held_fixed; independence_of_material_change_evidence; material_change_test_result_independence; domain_mismatch.

Rules enforced: Artifact 1 Section 7.2 (value definitions); Section 7.4 (material change); Rules 1, 3, 17, 19, 25, 28; Artifact 1 Section 13.2 (independence rating procedures).

Validation: Two independence rating procedures implemented as guided questionnaires. If Yes or No and Non_definitional, require full material-change block. If Not_tested but intervention_classification is not Not_applicable, refuse.

Panel 7: Scale-Separation Record
Fields: ratio; expansion_parameter; scale_microscopic; scale_collective; source_each; scale_separation_source_kind; scale_inference_source; unit_conversion_if_needed; minimum; band_declared; band_min_ratio; band_max_ratio; band_source; band_source_citation; dimensionless; control_parameter_value; control_parameter_source; analyst_dependence_acknowledged; analyst_dependence_note.

Rules enforced: Artifact 1 Section 7.5; Rule 7.

Validation: Compute ratio and expansion parameter. Check ratio against minimum. If source_kind = model_internal, warn STAG-Discovered unreachable. If band_source = analyst_chosen, set analyst_dependence_acknowledged = true and warn condition (b) fails. Compute band_min_ratio.

Panel 8: Partition Sensitivity and Identity-Splitting Audit
Fields: partition_sensitivity; alternative_partition_ids; partition_untested_flag; splitting_partition_id; splitting_would_change_label; splitting_audit_note; identity_partition_sensitive.

Rules enforced: Rule 7; Artifact 1 Sections 5.8, 7.8.

Validation: If merged and label above STAG-Unclassified, require identity-splitting audit. If new_node, require partition sensitivity instead. If splitting_would_change_label = true, set identity_partition_sensitive = true.

Panel 9: Derived Display Label and Evidential Anchoring
Fields computed: derived_display_label; evidential_anchoring or evidential_anchoring_status; unclassified_reason; not_determinable_flag; provisional_flag; threshold_sensitive_flag; regime_not_determinable; identity_partition_sensitive.

Rules enforced: Artifact 1 Section 7.6 (decision tree); Section 1.2 (four anchoring conditions); Rules 21, 26, 29, 30, 33; Section 7.10.

Validation: Compute label and anchoring status, display together. If any dependent field not_determinable, attach flag. If any dependent field inconclusive, attach provisional_flag. If STAG-Discovered, require anchoring status computed and displayed.

Panel 10: Extension-Tier Fields
Fields: threshold_provenance; characteristic_scale; reversibility; physical_status; graph_status; underlying_science_status; stag_implementation_status; statistical_gap_result; dependence_gap_discordance.

Rules enforced: Artifact 1 Sections 6, 8.6, 8.8, 9, 10.

Validation: Optional but required when applicable. If threshold_provenance populated, summary label must be consistent.

Panel 11: Composition, Derived-From, Revision, Supersession
Fields: composition; event_node; derived_from_source_node; derived_from_target_node; derivation_kind; derivation_specification; supersedes; superseded_by.

Rules enforced: Rules 10, 12, 13, 22; Artifact 1 Section 8.5.

Validation: If composite, require event node with at least two source nodes. If derived-from recorded, require derivation_kind and derivation_specification. Check supersession chains for cycles.

Panel 12: Evidence, Uncertainty, Annotator Provenance
Fields: evidence; uncertainty; alternative_classifications; annotator; protocol_cross_reference; confidence.

Rules enforced: Artifact 1 Section 14.1; Section 12.

Validation: Require annotator provenance and theory version before save. Require evidence for each core-tier field.

Panel 13: Save and Export
Actions: Validate entire record against JSON Schema, SHACL schema, and 32 semantic rules. If fail, display violations with rule numbers. If pass, save JSON. Optionally export PROV-O and SHACL report. Display label and anchoring status together with all flags.

Full Rule Enforcement Table (All 32 Rules)
Rule 1. Trigger: intervention_classification = Non_definitional and cross_domain_counterfactual_dependence = Yes or No. Action: Require model_reference, counterfactual_intervention, counterfactual_description, counterfactual_result, material_change_test, material_change_result.

Rule 2. Trigger: Precedence as in Section 7.2. Action: Apply precedence order.

Rule 3. Trigger: cross_domain_counterfactual_dependence = Yes. Action: Require source and target domains span at least two distinct declared domains.

Rule 4. Trigger: partition_kind = framework_level. Action: Force cross_domain_counterfactual_dependence = Untestable and unclassified_reason = inadmissible_partition.

Rule 5. Trigger: effective_description_change = Yes-strong and includes ΔAPP or ΔEFT. Action: Require external_justification.

Rule 6. Trigger: All domain entries. Action: Must belong to partition_registry_id and partition_version.

Rule 7. Trigger: derived_display_label = STAG-Discovered. Action: Require partition_sensitivity; scale_separation; ratio at or above minimum; source_kind = external_value or external_coefficient; band_declared, band_min_ratio, band_max_ratio; band_source; band_source_citation if external_reference; independence fields. If STAG-Definitional or STAG-Intra, require partition_sensitivity.

Rule 8. Trigger: Node identity. Action: Established from (S, M, G) alone, before transition attributes.

Rule 9. Trigger: Every annotation. Action: Declare tuple-matching rules, M-equivalence rule, granularity, partition justification before node identity finalized.

Rule 10. Trigger: Supersession. Action: Must be acyclic.

Rule 11. Trigger: Every annotation. Action: Identify theory, model, or scientific version.

Rule 12. Trigger: composition = composite. Action: Require event_node and at least two source_nodes.

Rule 13. Trigger: composition not composite. Action: event_node absent; self-loops carry regime_change.

Rule 14. Trigger: validity_regime. Action: Must not be consulted when determining node identity.

Rule 15. Trigger: Regime attribute. Action: Required for every node. If symmetric, broken, or crossover-band, require order_parameter, control_parameter_point, phase_diagram_source, domain_specific_label, framework_value_mapping. If crossover-band, require value_bands_if_crossover, regime_band_source, regime_band_analyst_chosen.

Rule 16. Trigger: Two descriptions share S, M, G. Action: node_identity must be merged.

Rule 17. Trigger: Not_tested. Action: Permitted only when intervention_classification = Not_applicable. Intervention performed with no result recorded is validation error. Intervention performed with result but uncertain material-change classification requires Uncertain.

Rule 18. Trigger: intervention_classification = Definitional or Definitional(expertise-dependent). Action: Require cited_structural_result with result_reference, applicability_conditions, conditions_check (each condition plus condition_witness). Witness must name specific equation, term, kernel, parameter range, or regime condition and cite source. General property only is validation error. If any condition lacks witness, force E4 and Definitional(expertise-dependent). If numerical result cited for Non_definitional, require cited_numerical_result with citation, result_summary, classification_effect, citation_scope.

Rule 19. Trigger: cross_domain_counterfactual_dependence = Intra_domain. Action: intervention_source_domains non-empty, contained within single declared domain; intervention_target_domain same domain; cross_domain_intervention_available populated.

Rule 20. Trigger: regime_attribute.value = not_determinable. Action: Record regime_not_determinable = true; retain label with flag.

Rule 21. Trigger: derived_display_label = STAG-Unclassified. Action: unclassified_reason populated and displayed.

Rule 22. Trigger: Structural relation between two M's (integration_out or truncation). Action: Record as derived-from edge, not M-equivalence.

Rule 23. Trigger: effective_description_change = Yes-weak. Action: derived_display_label = STAG-Unclassified with unclassified_reason = weak_effective_description_basis.

Rule 24. Trigger: Merged decision on two descriptions with different Lagrangians. Action: m_equivalence_basis and m_equivalence_witness both populated.

Rule 25. Trigger: domain_mismatch. Action: True if and only if intervention_target_domain not in set of domains to which source and target nodes are assigned under declared partition_id and partition_version.

Rule 26. Trigger: agreement_outcome = inconclusive for any core-tier field on which derived label depends. Action: derived label reported with provisional_flag = true.

Rule 27. Trigger: cross_domain_counterfactual_dependence = Intra_domain and material-change classification = Uncertain. Action: derived_display_label = STAG-Unclassified with unclassified_reason = uncertain.

Rule 28. Trigger: material_change_test = class change. Action: material_change_test_justification must state classification scheme.

Rule 29. Trigger: evidential_anchoring_status (STAG-Discovered only). Action: anchored if and only if all four conditions; anchored_with_stated_limitations if all four but at least one flagged interpretive or convention-dependent; preliminary if used to develop or illustrate codebook; candidate if proposed as possible instance. Operational: condition (a) cited_numerical_result.citation_scope = annotated_model or annotator computation; condition (b) band_source = external_reference, band_source_citation populated, band_min_ratio at or above minimum; condition (c) independence_of_material_change_evidence = independent; condition (d) material_change_test_result_independence = independent.

Rule 30. Trigger: Non-STAG-Discovered annotations. Action: evidential_anchoring_status = not_applicable or not_assessed.

Rule 31. Trigger: defining_coupling_intervention = true. Action: Second independent rater required; case excluded from STAG-Discovered unless second rater confirms intervention classification and material-change result.

Rule 32. Trigger: agreement_outcome differs between 0.5 and 0.7 thresholds. Action: threshold_sensitive_flag = true; falsification status of dependent label reported as threshold-dependent.

Rule 33. Trigger: Any field marked not_determinable because load-bearing source cannot be verified. Action: Label retained with not_determinable flag attached and displayed alongside; flag recorded under not_determinable_flag.

Core Logic as Executable Pseudocode
7.1 Display Label Derivation (Artifact 1, Section 7.6)
function deriveDisplayLabel(record):

Step 1. If record.effective_description_change == "No": return null (no transition recorded).

Step 2. If record.effective_description_change == "Uncertain": return {label: "STAG-Unclassified", reason: "uncertain"}.

Step 3. If record.effective_description_change == "Yes-weak": return {label: "STAG-Unclassified", reason: "weak_effective_description_basis"}.

Step 4 (Yes-strong). Set cfd = record.cross_domain_counterfactual_dependence; ic = record.intervention_classification; ss = record.scale_separation.

Step 4a. If cfd == "Intra_domain": if record.material_change_classification == "Uncertain" return {label: "STAG-Unclassified", reason: "uncertain"}; if ic in ["Definitional", "Definitional(expertise-dependent)"] return {label: "STAG-Intra-Definitional"}; if ic == "Non_definitional" return {label: "STAG-Intra-Non_definitional"}; if ic == "Not_applicable" return {label: "STAG-Intra"}.

Step 4b. If ic in ["Definitional", "Definitional(expertise-dependent)"] and isCrossDomain(record): return {label: "STAG-Definitional"}.

Step 4c. If ic == "Non_definitional" and cfd == "Yes" and scaleSeparationSatisfies(ss): return {label: "STAG-Discovered", anchoring: deriveAnchoringStatus(record)}.

Step 4d. If cfd == "Yes" and (ss is null or ss.source_kind == "model_internal" or ss.ratio < ss.minimum): if ss is null return {label: "STAG-Unclassified", reason: "insufficient_scale_separation"}; return {label: "STAG-Unclassified", reason: "model_internal_scale_separation"}.

Step 4e. If cfd == "No": return {label: "STAG-None"}.

Step 4f. If cfd == "Not_tested": return {label: "STAG-Unclassified", reason: "not_tested"}.

Step 4g. If cfd == "Untestable": return {label: "STAG-Unclassified", reason: "untestable_model or inadmissible_partition"}.

Step 4h. If cfd == "Uncertain": return {label: "STAG-Unclassified", reason: "uncertain"}.

Step 4i. If cfd == "not_determinable" or ic == "not_determinable": if isCrossDomain(record) return {label: "STAG-Definitional", not_determinable_flag: true}; if scaleSeparationSatisfies(ss) return {label: "STAG-Discovered", not_determinable_flag: true, anchoring: deriveAnchoringStatus(record)}.

7.2 Evidential Anchoring Status (Artifact 1, Section 1.2; Rule 29)
function deriveAnchoringStatus(record):

If record.derived_display_label is not "STAG-Discovered": return "not_applicable" or "not_assessed".

Set cond_a = (record.cited_numerical_result.citation_scope == "annotated_model") or record.material_change_computed_by_annotator.

Set cond_b = (record.scale_separation.band_source == "external_reference") and (record.scale_separation.band_source_citation is populated) and (record.scale_separation.band_min_ratio >= record.scale_separation.minimum).

Set cond_c = (record.independence_of_material_change_evidence == "independent").

Set cond_d = (record.material_change_test_result_independence == "independent").

If cond_a and cond_b and cond_c and cond_d: if anyConditionFlaggedInterpretive(record) return "anchored_with_stated_limitations"; return "anchored".

If record.used_to_develop_codebook: return "preliminary".

If record.proposed_as_possible_instance: return "candidate".

Return "preliminary" (default for unanchored STAG-Discovered).

7.3 Entailment Basis Decision Tree (Artifact 1, Section 7.3)
function determineEntailmentBasis(intervention, sources):

Step 1. If not setsTermOrKernelToZero(intervention): continue.

Step 2. If followsFromSymbolicFormAlone(intervention): return "E1".

Step 3. If hasCitableResult(intervention, sources): conditions = getApplicabilityConditions(intervention, sources); for c in conditions: if not hasWitness(c) return "E4"; if anyConditionUnconfirmableOrContested(conditions) return "E4"; return "E2".

Step 4. If not hasCitableResult(intervention, sources): return "E3".

Step 5. If cannotDecide(intervention, sources): logForSecondRater(); return "not_determinable".

If not sourcesVerifiable(sources): return "not_determinable".

7.4 Scale-Separation Satisfaction (Artifact 1, Section 7.5)
function scaleSeparationSatisfies(ss):

If ss is null: return false.

If ss.source_kind == "model_internal": return false.

If ss.ratio < ss.minimum: return false.

If ss.source_kind == "external_value": return ss.has_external_scale_value.

If ss.source_kind == "external_coefficient": return ss.has_external_coefficient and ss.band_declared.

Return false.

7.5 Partition Audit (Artifact 1, Sections 5.8, 7.7, 7.8)
function runPartitionAudit(record):

Set label = record.derived_display_label.

If label in ["STAG-Unclassified", "STAG-None"]: return (audit not required).

If label in ["STAG-Discovered", "STAG-Definitional", "STAG-Intra", "STAG-Intra-Definitional", "STAG-Intra-Non_definitional"]: require record.partition_sensitivity; require record.alternative_partition_ids.length >= 1; recomputeLabelsUnderAlternativePartitions(record).

If record.node_identity == "merged" and label above STAG-Unclassified: require record.splitting_partition_id; require record.splitting_would_change_label (boolean); require record.splitting_audit_note; if record.splitting_would_change_label set record.identity_partition_sensitive = true.

If record.partition.intra_domain_rate > 0.60: triggerAuditProcedure(record.partition).

7.6 M-Equivalence Validation (Artifact 1, Section 5.3; Rule 24)
function validateMEquivalence(record):

If record.node_identity == "merged": if record.descriptions.have_different_lagrangians: if not record.m_equivalence_basis or not record.m_equivalence_witness raise ValidationError("Rule 24: merged decision on different Lagrangians requires both m_equivalence_basis and m_equivalence_witness"); if record.m_equivalence_basis not in ["field_redefinition", "basis_change", "gauge_fixing", "exact_duality"] raise ValidationError("M-equivalence restricted to exact reparametrizations").

7.7 Derived-From vs. M-Equivalence (Rule 22)
function classifyStructuralRelation(relation):

If relation.kind in ["integration_out", "truncation"]: if relation.is_exact_effective_action return "M_equivalence"; else return "derived_from".

Return "M_equivalence".

